 r←{development}CheckPackagesForBetterVersions flag;pkgs;latest;data;header;parms;allOnTatin;bool;path;report;msg
⍝ Checks whether there is a better version of the packages available in the packages/ folder,
⍝ but check the optional left argument `development`.
⍝ Note that this function only checks [tatin] (the principal Tatin registry)
⍝ `flag` is an insurance against accidental calls.
⍝ `development` defaults to 0, meaning that the folder packages/ is investigated.
⍝ You can change that by passing a 1 as left argument; then packages_dev/ is investigated instead.
 r←''
 :If flag
     'Run #.Tatin.Admin.Initialize_Client before calling this function'Assert 9=##.FilesAndDirs.⎕NC'APLTreeUtils2'
     development←{0<⎕NC ⍵:⍎⍵ ⋄ 0}'development'
     path←##.CiderConfig.HOME,(1+development)⊃'/packages' '/packages_dev'
     :If 0<≢pkgs←##.FilesAndDirs.ListDirs path
         pkgs←{⊃,/1↓⎕NPARTS ⍵}¨pkgs
         parms←⎕NS''
         parms.latest←1
         allOnTatin←,parms ⎕SE.Tatin.ListPackages'[tatin]'
         bool←(##.Registry.RemoveMinorAndPatch¨allOnTatin)∊##.Registry.RemoveMinorAndPatch¨pkgs
         allOnTatin←bool/allOnTatin
         report←⍪(~allOnTatin∊pkgs)/allOnTatin
         report,←(~pkgs∊allOnTatin)/pkgs
         :If 0<≢report
             header←'Current' 'Latest'
             report←(header,[0.5]' ')⍪report
             report[2;]←(⌈/⍉≢¨report[;1 2])⍴¨'='
             report←⍕report
             report,[1]←' '
             msg←'=> Use the function ReinstallAndUpdateTatinPackages if udating is required'
             report←((≢msg)⌈2⊃⍴report)↑[2]report
             report,[1]←msg
             ⍞←report
             ⍞←⎕UCS 10
         :Else
             ⍞←'All up-to-date',⎕UCS 10
         :EndIf
     :Else
         ⍞←'The given folder does not contain any sub-folders',⎕UCS 10
     :EndIf
 :EndIf
⍝Done
